. do "20250722_213235_01agbe_h4.do"

. **************************************************************************
. * H4: Gender heterogeneity – Triple‐Difference DiD Analysis               *
. * Authors: [REDACTED], [REDACTED]                                        *
. * Based on pre-analysis plan (Lenzi & Román, July 14, 2025)                 *
. * Hypothesis: Having daughters increases support for gender equality more   *
. * for women than men (Triple Difference)                                   *
. **************************************************************************
. * CHANGE LOG (July 2025):
. * Following the request from the study organizers, this version reports 
. * a single regression-based result for Hypothesis 4. 
. * 
. * We use the variable `id_gnorm_eq`, capturing agreement with the 
. * statement: "Best if man and woman work the same amount so they can 
. * share the responsibility".
. * 
. * This item is the most general and directly interpretable measure of 
. * gender egalitarianism in roles, making it the most conceptually 
. * appropriate outcome to test whether daughters shift beliefs more in 
. * men than women.
. **************************************************************************/
. * clear all
. version 18

. set maxvar 10000


. 
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * INSTALL PACKAGES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. ssc install mdesc
checking mdesc consistency and verifying not already installed...
all files already exist and are up to date.

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * CONFIGURE FILE PATHS  (Please do not change)
. /*
> * the following code automatically sets paths based on where you saved the di
> stributed file-package on your system *
> *-----------------------------
> 
> if strpos("`c(pwd)'", "code") {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'/.."
> }
> else {
> global ROOT "`c(pwd)'"
> }
> global IN "$ROOT/data/raw" // folder, in which the original datasets are stor
> ed
> global DATA "$ROOT/data/derived" // folder for datasets
> global OUT "$ROOT/out" // folder for output (results, tables)
> 
> */
. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation * 
. * ============================
. 
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. *----------------------------------------------------------------------------
. 
. use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
. * Merge ppathl with all datasets, that you deem relevant for your analysis. (
> Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the using datase
> t; the default is all.)
. 
. * biobirth contains information on fertility history
. merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are consolida
> ted from different sources
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
. merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable inputdataset was str6, now str9 to accommodate using data's values)
(label cid already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the household int
> erview; use for household net income
. merge m:1 hid syear using "$IN/hgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) keepusin
> g(hid syear hghinc)
(label iyear already defined)
(label iyear_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
. label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
. save "$DATA/h4_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
file C:\Users\dalbrecht\Research
    Projects\ManyDaughters\ManyDaughters_DataPreprocessing/data/derived_confi
    > dential/5%-sample/h4_dataset.dta saved

. *-----------------------------
. *  Construct outcome
. *     id_gnorm_eq
. *-----------------------------
. *......................................
. * Dependent variables 
. *......................................
. 
. mvdecode plh0308_v1 plh0308_v2, mv(-10/-1) // missing values coded as negativ
> e to missing
  plh0308_v1: 26743 missing values generated
  plh0308_v2: 25835 missing values generated

. 
. 
. * Transform variables such that the lowest value is most in accordance with t
> raditional gender norms, i.e. disagreeing on an egalitarian taks distribution
>  
. replace plh0308_v1 = 5 - plh0308_v1
(363 real changes made)

. gen id_gnorm_eq = plh0308_v1 > 2 & plh0308_v1 != .

. replace id_gnorm_eq = 1 if id_gnorm_eq == 0 & plh0308_v2 > 4 & plh0308_v2 != 
> .
(878 real changes made)

. label variable id_gnorm_eq "Agree with: Best if man and woman work the same a
> mount"

. 
. 
. 
. *  Construct DiD regressors 
. *-----------------------------
. bysort pid: egen byte Daughter = max(kidsex01==2)

. bysort pid: egen byte Son      = max(kidsex01==1)

. bysort pid (syear): assert Daughter==Daughter[1]

. gen int   yearFirstChild = kidgeb01

. gen byte  Post             = (syear >= kidgeb01) if Daughter==1 | Son==1
(10,637 missing values generated)

. gen byte  Man              = (sex==1)

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * Controls (PaP Table 4)
. *-----------------------------
. mdesc sumkids pgfamstd plh0258_h sampreg birthregion_ew bioage migback pgbilz
> eit hghinc pgemplst pgexpft

    Variable    |     Missing          Total     Percent Missing
----------------+-----------------------------------------------
        sumkids |           0         35,228           0.00
       pgfamstd |       7,823         35,228          22.21
      plh0258_h |       8,122         35,228          23.06
        sampreg |           0         35,228           0.00
   birthregio~w |           0         35,228           0.00
         bioage |           0         35,228           0.00
        migback |           0         35,228           0.00
      pgbilzeit |       7,823         35,228          22.21
         hghinc |       4,207         35,228          11.94
       pgemplst |       7,823         35,228          22.21
        pgexpft |       7,823         35,228          22.21
----------------+-----------------------------------------------

. 
. gen nchild = sumkids

. replace nchild = 5 if nchild > 5
(412 real changes made)

. 
. gen mastat = pgfamstd == 1 | pgfamstd == 6 | pgfamstd == 7 | pgfamstd == 8

. replace mastat = . if pgfamstd == .
(7,823 real changes made, 7,823 to missing)

. label define mastat 0 "Unmarried" 1 "Married"

. label values mastat mastat

. 
. replace sampreg = sampreg - 1
(35,228 real changes made)

. replace birthregion_ew = birthregion_ew - 1
(35,228 real changes made)

. label define ew 0 "West" 1 "East"

. label values sampreg ew

. label values birthregion_ew ew

. 
. sort pid piyear

. gen age = syear - gebjahr

. gen age_sq = age^2

. 
. gen exp = pgexpft
(7,823 missing values generated)

. gen exp_sq = exp^2
(7,823 missing values generated)

. 
. gen byte emplyd = inlist(pgemplst,1,2)

. label define emp 0 "Not employed" 1 "Employed"

. label values emplyd emp

. 
. label variable hghinc "Household net income"

. global controls "i.nchild i.mastat i.sampreg age age_sq exp exp_sq i.migback 
> pgbilzeit hghinc i.emplyd"

. 
. *-----------------------------
. * Sample Restrictions
. *-----------------------------
. keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
(4,698 observations deleted)

. keep if sampreg >= 0 & inrange(age,18,50)
(14,445 observations deleted)

. keep if yearFirstChild > 0
(4,839 observations deleted)

. keep if inlist(syear, 2012, 2018)
(9,993 observations deleted)

. keep if inrange(yearFirstChild, 2013, 2017)
(1,137 observations deleted)

. 
. bysort pid: egen byte has_eq_pre = max(!missing(id_gnorm_eq) & !Post & syear=
> =2012)

. bysort pid: egen byte has_eq_post = max(!missing(id_gnorm_eq) & Post & syear=
> =2018)

. 
. 
. *-----------------------------
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4 *
. *-----------------------------
. * Model Description:
. * We test whether having a firstborn daughter increases support for gender eq
> uality 
. * more for men than for women using a triple-difference design.
. * 
. * Model: y = β₀ + β₁Man + β₂Daughter + β₃Post + β₄Man×Daughter + β₅Man×Post +
>  
. *            β₆Daughter×Post + β₇Man×Daughter×Post + γX + ε
. *
. * Key hypothesis: H₀: β₄ + β₇ = 0 vs H₁: β₄ + β₇ > 0
. * This tests whether the effect of having a daughter is larger for men than w
> omen.
. 
. * Create results file
.     
. 
. keep if has_eq_pre & has_eq_post
(78 observations deleted)

. 
. * Run triple-difference regression
. reg id_gnorm_eq i.Man##i.Daughter##i.Post $controls, vce(cluster cid)

Linear regression                               Number of obs     =         33
                                                F(10, 11)         =          .
                                                Prob > F          =          .
